# Line endings.
#
# Everything in this repository is LF, in the index and in the working tree.
# `llmproxy/server.py` was the lone CRLF file for a long time, which is the
# kind of thing nobody notices until a tool rewrites the file and produces a
# 22,000-line diff that buries the actual change. Declaring it here means git
# normalizes on checkout and commit regardless of the editor or platform a
# contributor uses, so the anomaly cannot come back.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary files and leave them alone; `eol=lf` fixes
# the working-tree ending for the files it does treat as text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only script types would need CRLF to run. None exist today; these are
# here so adding one later does not silently get normalized into something
# cmd.exe mishandles.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
